    "id": "p41-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Solve $5\\cot^2 x-2\\operatorname{cosec}x+2=0$ for $0<x<2\\pi$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "worked": "Using $\\cot^2x=\\operatorname{cosec}^2x-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}5(\\operatorname{cosec}^2x-1)-2\\operatorname{cosec}x+2&=0\\\\5\\operatorname{cosec}^2x-2\\operatorname{cosec}x-3&=0\\\\(5\\operatorname{cosec}x+3)(\\operatorname{cosec}x-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\operatorname{cosec}x=-\\frac35$ or $\\operatorname{cosec}x=1$. The first value is impossible because $|\\operatorname{cosec}x|\\ge1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x&=1\\\\x&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nThis lies in $0<x<2\\pi$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
